 "sections": [
  {
   "heading": "Posture controls",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "kind": "p",
     "text": "Posture controls determine how a ship will operate and maneuver and which sensor and defensive systems are enabled."
    },
    {
     "kind": "table",
     "rows": [
      [
       "Display",
       "Full name",
       "Settings"
      ],
      [
       "THRTL",
       "Throttle Control",
       "1/3: Ship will move at 1/3 of max speed. 2/3: Ship will move at 2/3 of max speed. FULL: Ship will move at max speed. FLANK: Ship will move above max speed. Causes damage to engines. FQ (carriers only): speed is limited so spacecraft can take off and land. While heading and velocity stay within the green-deck angle (default 7.5 degrees) the cap is about one-third of max speed; otherwise it drops to a 5 m/s crawl."
      ],
      [
       "MNVR",
       "Maneuvering Posture",
       "DIRECT: Ship will move in a straight line. EVADE: Ship will make random course changes to attempt to avoid incoming fire."
      ],
      [
       "FORM",
       "Formation Positioning",
       "REL: Ships will have the same orientation of the guide ship. The guide will wait for other ships to catch up. TRU: Escorts keep the same true bearing and distance from the guide when the guide turns. They are still steered to the guide's heading. The guide will wait for other ships to catch up. LOOSE: The guide will not wait for other ships to catch up."
      ],
      [
       "BSHRT",
       "Battle-Short",
       "OFF: Continuous-use equipment that honors battle short (beams, jammers, illuminators, dazzlers) shuts down for cooldown once its own burst duration is exceeded, at 7.5 seconds for the Mk600 and Mk610 beams and anywhere from 40 to 180 seconds for electronic-warfare sets. ON: Continuous-use equipment that honors battle short (beams, jammers, illuminators, dazzlers) keeps running past its own burst duration; each second past the limit it has a per-component chance to take self-damage. The Mk610, for example, rolls a 60% chance of 20 damage starting after 7.5 seconds"
      ],
      [
       "RADAR",
       "Radar Emissions Control",
       "ON: Ship sensors are active. OFF: Ship sensors are inactive. -25% signature."
      ],
      [
       "COMM",
       "Communications Emissions Control",
       "XMIT: Ship comms are active. RECV: Ship sensors are inactive. -10% signature."
      ],
      [
       "ESUPT",
       "Electronic Support Modules",
       "ON: Passive electronic-support sensors operate. OFF: Passive sensors are switched off, so this ship generates no new passive tracks. This does not reduce signature. It can be used to cut clutter once a track is held."
      ],
      [
       "WCON",
       "Weapons Control",
       "FREE: Ship will automatically return fire with non-missile weapons on targets that are firing at them. TIGHT: Ship will not attack except when given a target. HOLD: Ship will not attack, and dual-purpose weapons hold fire. Dedicated point-defense turrets, defensive missiles, and decoys still operate. Turrets will still bear on any current target."
      ],
      [
       "PDTRT",
       "Point Defenses - Turrets",
       "AUTO: Dedicated point defense turrets and dual-purpose weapons will target the closest missiles. DEDI: Dedicated point defense turrets will target the closest missiles. MAN: Point defense turrets will only shoot at designated missiles."
      ],
      [
       "PDSML",
       "Point Defenses - Missiles",
       "Controls the firing of interceptor missiles. Click to open policy settings."
      ],
      [
       "DECOY",
       "Point Defenses - Decoys",
       "LEAST: Only the lowest-capability decoy necessary to defeat a given threat will be deployed. If the missile type is unknown all decoys will be fired. BEST: Only the highest-capability decoy necessary to defeat a given threat will be deployed. If the missile type is unknown all decoys will be fired. AUTO: All decoys compatible with the threat will be deployed. If the missile type is unknown all decoys will be fired. MAN: Decoys can only be deployed manually via the Action Menu."
      ],
      [
       "PDZNE",
       "Point Defense Zone",
       "AREA: Point defenses will target all missiles, prioritizing the ones threatening the ship. POINT: Point defenses will target only missiles threatening the ship."
      ]
     ],
