  {
   "heading": "Integrity rating",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "kind": "p",
     "text": "A ship's integrity directly affects how resistant its components are to damage. Lots of empty space means less structural members to absorb damage and protect components. A ship with at least 60% of its slots filled (mounts, compartments, and modules) gets the full hull Damage Reduction. From 60% down to 20% fill the protection falls linearly, and at 20% fill or less it is 25% of the hull value."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "heading": "Ship hulls",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "kind": "p",
     "text": "Ship hulls determine a ship's base stats as well as how many components it can have."
    }
   ]
  },
